cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this code, notebook, or framework in your research,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: >
  HGT_GBD-Mortality: Spatial Predictive Modelling of Cause-Specific
  NCD Mortality in East Africa Using Heterogeneous Graph Transformers
abstract: >
  A Heterogeneous Graph Transformer (HGT) framework for detecting
  spatial predictive patterns in cause-specific non-communicable
  disease (NCD) mortality — hypertensive heart disease (HHD),
  ischaemic heart disease (IHD), stroke, and diabetes — across five
  East African countries (Burundi, Kenya, Rwanda, Tanzania, Uganda)
  using Global Burden of Disease (GBD) data spanning 1990–2023.

  The framework implements two graph configurations: Graph A
  (both-sex × age × country, 80 nodes) and Graph B
  (male/female × age × country, 160 nodes), each estimated under
  three covariate specifications (SDI-only, Risk-only, Full).

  Key methodological features include: multi-seed evaluation
  (seeds = [42, 123, 456, 789, 1024]); bootstrap 95% confidence
  intervals; CI-based reliability classification; OLS spatial lag
  and Maximum Likelihood Spatial Lag (CAR-type) benchmarks;
  Moran's I permutation test on residuals; degradation diagnostic
  (training loss curves, gradient L2 norms); ablation study;
  rolling temporal window validation; attention weight analysis
  (node embedding norms); and Monte Carlo GBD uncertainty
  propagation.

  Implementation: Python 3.10, PyTorch, PyTorch Geometric (HGTConv),
  NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn, libpysal, esda, matplotlib.
  Designed for Google Colab with GPU acceleration.
  Hidden dimension: 64; Attention heads: 4; HGTConv layers: 2;
  Learning rate: 0.003; Weight decay: 1e-4; Dropout: 0.2;
  Epochs: 200.
